      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "@{5a5bcc5dc99a62652a829a15|full_name}: Possibly. But as I understand it, voice chat is piped through a peer-to-peer service, so there's no load on the actual server. As for performance, the main bottleneck seems to be the spatialized audio, so if voice calls were in-head/non-spatialized, then it wouldn't be so bad.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
